  "notes": [
   "Each LED unit: resistor bridges the breadboard centre gap in column c (bank b row f to bank t row e); LED anode in column c bank b (row h), cathode in column c+1 bank b (row h); a black wire runs from column c+1 bank b (row i) to the top negative rail (tn); signal wire from column c bank t (row b) to a Mega digital pin.",
   "Pin mapping follows the circuit image: pin 13 -> column 2, 12 -> 4, 11 -> 6, 10 -> 8, 9 -> 10, 8 -> 12, 7 -> 15, 6 -> 17, 5 -> 20, 4 -> 23, 3 -> 26, 2 -> 28.",
   "The image's breadboard has rows f-j in the upper section and a-e in the lower; the catalogue naming (bank 't' = a-e, 'b' = f-j) is used, so the LED/ground side is bank b and the signal side is bank t.",
   "Rail hole numbers (tn.<n>) are approximate; the whole tn rail is one strip so the exact hole does not change connectivity.",
   "Mega GND next to AREF is mapped to GND.1; the black wire connects it to the top negative rail, which grounds all LED cathodes.",
   "Resistor value 220 ohm per the manual; the type's default label is 100 ohm so the value prop is set per instance."
  ]
 },
